{
  // Blocking SCA gate for the Expo / React Native mobile app (npm lockfile).
  // Fails CI on high/critical advisories. See docs/SUPPLY_CHAIN.md.
  //
  // Runtime vs. development dependencies:
  //   - PRODUCTION deps (react-native, @react-navigation/*, expo-* — the code
  //     actually bundled onto the device by EAS/Expo) carry NO high/critical
  //     advisory. A new high/critical in a shipped dependency MUST fail this job.
  //   - The allowlisted advisories below are all in code that runs on a
  //     developer's or EAS build machine, never inside the Metro bundle
  //     installed on a device. Each documents why no bump clears it.
  //
  // brace-expansion is NOT allowlisted: it is forced to 5.0.12 via a blanket
  // npm `override` in package.json. 5.0.10 and 5.0.11 are the patched versions
  // for the two stack-exhaustion advisories (GHSA-6j4f-fj2g-mc7p and
  // GHSA-qhr7-859c-m2p7, both high, published 2026-09-29), which supersede the
  // earlier GHSA-3jxr-9vmj-r5cp / GHSA-mh99-v99m-4gvg pair the override was
  // first added for. serve-handler's minimatch@3 still tolerates the 5.x export
  // shape because our rewrite patterns contain no braces, so expand() is never
  // invoked. The uuid moderate sits below this high+ gate. Keep the allowlist
  // minimal so a genuinely new high/critical still fails the job.
  //
  // Each exception documents owner + reason + review date. Prune an entry once
  // its dependency is bumped past the patched version.
  "high": true,
  "allowlist": [
    // (GHSA-5xrq-8626-4rwp pruned 2026-10-31: vitest is now 4.1.12, outside its
    // <=3.2.5 range — the vitest 4 upgrade that replaced Renovate's #825.)
    // (GHSA-fx2h-pf6j-xcff pruned 2026-10-24: the blanket vite override to
    // 6.4.4 — added for GHSA-587h-7wmj-h5pm — is past its <=6.4.2 range.)
    // (GHSA-86w9-cpqp-85rv pruned 2026-10-31: node-forge is now 1.4.2, outside its
    // <=1.4.0 range — the bump that cleared the five 2026-10-30 node-forge highs.)
    // (GHSA-vfj7-8cjw-p6xm pruned 2026-11-07: GitHub withdrew the braces advisory on 2026-10-23, so it no longer matches.)
    // (GHSA-mrhx-c7xc-m3w5 pruned 2026-11-07: zod left the tree with the Expo SDK 57 patch update, #849.)
  ],
  "report-type": "summary"
}
